# Greenfinger configuration.
#
# Read two ways, and both find this file. The launchers source it before starting the jvm, so
# every GF_* here is an environment variable; and application.yml imports it with
# spring.config.import, so a main class started from an IDE -- no launcher, no exported
# variables -- reads exactly the same values. Keep it to plain KEY=value: it is parsed as a
# properties file in the second case, which does not understand `export` or shell quoting.
#
# Copy to .env beside run-local.sh and change what you need. Everything here has a working default
# in config/application.yml, so an empty .env is a valid one -- and a secret written here never
# reaches the repository.

# ---- Which profile. dev is zero configuration; prod is your own database and stores. ----
# GF_PROFILE=dev

# ---- Database. dev defaults to an H2 file: nothing to install. prod requires these. ----
# GF_DB_URL=jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/greenfinger?currentSchema=public
# GF_DB_USERNAME=greenfinger
# GF_DB_PASSWORD=
# GF_DB_DRIVER=org.postgresql.Driver
# MySQL:  jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/greenfinger?useUnicode=true&characterEncoding=utf8&serverTimezone=UTC
#         com.mysql.cj.jdbc.Driver
# SQLite: jdbc:sqlite:./data/.state/greenfinger.db  with  org.sqlite.JDBC, and the only database
#         that needs its dialect named, because Hibernate ships none for it:
# GF_DB_DIALECT=org.hibernate.community.dialect.SQLiteDialect

# ---- The server: run-local.sh. The command line needs none of this and has no login. ----
# GF_SERVER_PORT=8080
# GF_API_PREFIX=/v2
# The two accounts, handed out up front: username:password:role, comma separated.
#   ADMIN    creates catalogs and runs crawl / update / rebuild / delete
#   SUPPORT  reads everything and changes nothing
# Change the passwords here. This file is never committed; the yml beside it is.
# GF_USERS=admin:admin123:ADMIN,tester:tester123:SUPPORT

# What sign-in tokens are signed with. Any long random string; the same one on every node, or a
# browser behind nginx will be asked to sign in again whenever it lands on a different one.
# Left unset, each process makes up its own and says so in the log.
#   openssl rand -base64 48
# GF_TOKEN_SECRET=
# GF_SECURITY_ENABLED=true
# GF_TOKEN_VALIDITY=8h
# Where the front end is served from. The Angular dev server during development; a build served
# by this same jar needs no entry.
# GF_CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:4200

# ---- Where the crawl puts things ----
# GF_DATA_DIR=./data
# GF_STATE_DIR=./data/.state
# GF_OUTPUT_TYPES=file            # file, index, vector -- combine with commas

# ---- Files: local disk, or MinIO with the identical layout ----
# GF_FILE_TARGET=local            # local | minio
# GF_MINIO_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:19000
# GF_MINIO_ACCESS_KEY=
# GF_MINIO_SECRET_KEY=
# GF_MINIO_BUCKET=greenfinger

# ---- Cluster. Nodes agreeing on the name find each other and share one crawl. ----
# greenfinger-cli.sh --cluster <name> sets this; "default" means two terminals on one
# machine are one cluster without anybody having to say so.
# GF_CLUSTER_NAME=default
# GF_CLUSTER_HOSTS=127.0.0.1
# GF_CLUSTER_PORT=22000

# ---- Full text search. Embedded by default: nothing to install. ----
# One index per catalog, named <prefix>-<catalog id>, holding every version of it.
# GF_INDEX_PROVIDER=lucene        # lucene | elasticsearch
# GF_INDEX_PREFIX=greenfinger
# GF_LUCENE_ANALYZER=standard     # standard | smartcn | cjk
#   standard is right for English, which is what is mostly crawled. smartcn is a real Chinese
#   segmenter -- the embedded counterpart of installing IK -- and cjk is bigrams, no dictionary.
# GF_LUCENE_COMMIT_EVERY=1000
# ---- ... or a real Elasticsearch, when one machine is not enough ----
# GF_ES_URIS=http://localhost:9200
# GF_ES_ANALYZER=standard         # ik_max_word and ik_smart need the IK plugin installed

# ---- Semantic and cross modal search. Embedded by default too. ----
# Lucene's HNSW is what Elasticsearch's own knn search is built on.
# GF_VECTOR_STORE=lucene          # lucene | qdrant | weaviate
# GF_LUCENE_SIMILARITY=cosine     # cosine | dot | euclidean
# GF_QDRANT_URL=http://localhost:6333
# GF_WEAVIATE_URL=http://localhost:18080/v1

# ---- Embeddings. "local" runs the models here: no account, no quota. ----
# GF_EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=local     # local | ollama | openai
# GF_MODEL_DIR=~/.greenfinger/models
# GF_EMBEDDING_OFFLINE=false      # refuse to download; fail instead if not cached
# GF_OLLAMA_URL=http://localhost:11434
# GF_OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen3-embedding:4b

# The only value that is genuinely secret. Needed solely for the openai provider.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# ---- Merge (update --refresh) ----
# Revisiting every known page needs room for all of them, so raise this before a merge.
# GF_MAX_FETCH_SIZE=100000

# ---- Javascript ----
# The default, adaptive, fetches over http and renders only the pages that came back empty, so a
# static site never starts a browser. Set restclient to never render, or name an engine to always.
# GF_EXTRACTOR=adaptive            # adaptive | restclient | htmlunit | playwright | selenium
# GF_ADAPTIVE_BROWSER=htmlunit     # which browser adaptive falls back to.
#                                  #   htmlunit   nothing to install, engine is in the jar
#                                  #   playwright better rendering; needs `playwright install`
#                                  #   selenium   better rendering; needs a browser on the machine

# ---- Crawl defaults ----
# GF_WORK_THREADS=16
# GF_MAX_FETCH_SIZE=10000
# GF_FETCH_INTERVAL=1000
# GF_MAX_VERSIONS=10
# GF_LOG_LEVEL=WARN

# The front end container's port and api address, how many nodes to start, which cluster to join,
# where the data goes: none of that is secret, so it is in run.conf beside this file instead.
# This one is only for what must not be committed.
